1
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:11,980
Welcome back! This is the last episode: show day, from the night before to the last cue.

2
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:18,090
The day before, open Settings, Tools, and press Check. Here, a new version is out.

3
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:25,220
Leave it for after the event. Installing closes LayerCue, and the audience screen goes dark.

4
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:35,020
Run the whole show once, on the real screens. A red card says a file is missing. Here, the welcome video was renamed.

5
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:40,370
Press Locate file on the card. Pick the file, and the card is relinked.

6
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:46,560
Listen to every video and song once, at show volume.

7
00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:52,210
In Settings, Stage, turn on Lock editing while live.

8
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:59,730
Now, while a screen is on, the first slide you send locks editing. The lock lights up in the status bar.

9
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:06,480
Slides still go out. But a stray drag can't move a card, or change a slide, mid-show.

10
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:13,560
It unlocks by itself when every screen is off. A lock you set by hand stays.

11
00:01:15,580 --> 00:01:22,050
If a cable comes out, LayerCue says so: Output screen disconnected. The on-air chip shows a ring.

12
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:26,750
Plug it back in, and it comes right back by itself.

13
00:01:27,820 --> 00:01:30,950
A message always says what happened, and what to do.

14
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:38,810
If LayerCue itself misbehaves, press Tell us what's wrong. Choose Question, Idea or Bug, and write what happened.

15
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:49,040
Make the booth easy on yourself. In Settings, General, choose large slide cards. They're harder to miss in a dark room.

16
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:58,020
Remember window layout is on to begin with. Set your windows up once in rehearsal, and show day opens the same way.

17
00:01:58,690 --> 00:02:04,810
The screens you switched on are remembered too. Open LayerCue, and they come back on by themselves.

18
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:13,010
One last pass before the doors open: every screen on, the right layers shown, no red cards, and the sound checked.

19
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:19,000
You can now run a show, from the night before to the last cue.

20
00:02:19,670 --> 00:02:25,080
When a new version ships, a What's New episode joins this playlist. Thanks for watching!

